1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:06,589
A typhoon is coming soon.

2
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:08,758
Because of it, a landslide will occur.

3
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:12,262
Those five you are
so close with will all die.

4
00:00:14,931 --> 00:00:16,558
Mr. Nishigami?

5
00:00:16,641 --> 00:00:20,020
Let me tell you what will happen
if you break the code.

6
00:00:20,103 --> 00:00:21,563
Every human involved with you

7
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:24,941
will have all Grim Reaper
related memories erased.

8
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:25,984
And of course,

9
00:00:26,067 --> 00:00:29,904
you yourself will be punished
by the laws of the underworld.

10
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:31,322
Such a thing is impossible!

11
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:33,992
The typhoon passes through multiple areas.

12
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:35,368
Up on that mountain,

13
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,495
there is an old shrine nobody visits.

14
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:42,000
All natural disasters around here
are governed by that shrine.

15
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:45,795
If you go there, you may
be able to change something.

16
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:50,216
A Grim Reaper in human form?

17
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:52,218
A Grim Reaper…

18
00:00:52,302 --> 00:00:53,803
Are you here to collect me?

19
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,221
I'm sorry.

20
00:00:55,305 --> 00:00:57,432
I can't die. Yeah.

21
00:00:58,099 --> 00:01:00,810
Because I'm a god.

22
00:01:05,774 --> 00:01:09,569
Well now, what do you need from me today?

23
00:01:11,154 --> 00:01:12,322
Who are you?

24
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:17,494
Japan is home to myriad gods,

25
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:22,707
and their origins trace back
to the nature worship of the Jomon period.

26
00:01:22,791 --> 00:01:27,629
As for me, the wind, water,
clouds, rain, lightning…

27
00:01:28,922 --> 00:01:31,841
I control all weather!

28
00:01:31,925 --> 00:01:34,427
I am an ancient god of Japan!

29
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:37,138
The venerable Dragon God!

30
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:39,891
DRAGON GOD

31
00:01:41,726 --> 00:01:43,019
Dragon God.

32
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,355
Yes, well…

33
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:47,273
That aside,

34
00:01:47,357 --> 00:01:52,028
what is a handsome young Reaper
like you doing here in the mountains…

35
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,363
Oh, right.

36
00:01:53,446 --> 00:01:56,366
There's a typhoon today, right?
You must be busy too.

37
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:01,996
I am sorry for the sudden visit.

38
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:05,917
I need to ask you a favor.

39
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:07,710
Okay.

40
00:02:09,045 --> 00:02:11,756
Then, shall I at least hear you out?

41
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,091
What is it?

42
00:02:15,009 --> 00:02:16,219
The landslide.

43
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,142
I want you to prevent it.

44
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,228
What?

45
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:27,605
Why?

46
00:02:29,274 --> 00:02:31,943
There are humans I want to save.

47
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:34,737
Oh, I see.

48
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:35,780
Huh…

49
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:41,536
So those people are fated to die
in tonight's landslide?

50
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:43,246
Yes.

51
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:48,001
Five young humans
have been marked for death.

52
00:02:48,918 --> 00:02:50,962
Those people haven't…

53
00:02:51,963 --> 00:02:53,047
done much.

54
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:55,925
Really…

55
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,557
They haven't achieved anything at all.

56
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,600
But this summer…

57
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,271
many things happened…

58
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:11,566
at that villa.

59
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:16,321
I think,

60
00:03:17,697 --> 00:03:19,407
throughout this vacation…

61
00:03:21,701 --> 00:03:23,620
they all discovered something.

62
00:03:36,549 --> 00:03:40,428
"I want to protect
those young people's future."

63
00:03:40,511 --> 00:03:44,140
I guess that's what
you're trying to say, but…

64
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:48,311
That isn't something
a Grim Reaper should say.

65
00:03:49,604 --> 00:03:51,397
But, I…

66
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,192
Look.

67
00:03:54,984 --> 00:03:57,612
Today, without a doubt,
a landslide will occur.

68
00:03:57,695 --> 00:04:00,615
You cannot change that absolute fact.

69
00:04:01,574 --> 00:04:06,663
However, there is a place
that is safe from that disaster.

70
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:08,248
And I know where it is.

71
00:04:09,123 --> 00:04:10,708
It's right here.

72
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:16,047
Hundreds of years ago,
humans built a shrine here

73
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:18,383
because it was a safe place.

74
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:21,386
Rain pours down hard
on the top of this mountain.

75
00:04:21,469 --> 00:04:23,763
Then the flood comes rushing down.

76
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:24,806
However,

77
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:30,311
the water that comes out of the valley
above here splits into two directions.

78
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,354
And, what's more…

79
00:04:31,896 --> 00:04:34,107
Look around here. It's all bamboo.

80
00:04:34,190 --> 00:04:35,650
There is a bamboo grove.

81
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:39,028
It protects the ground.

82
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:42,532
They say bamboo roots
are all connected underground,

83
00:04:42,615 --> 00:04:43,491
like a net.

84
00:04:43,574 --> 00:04:49,664
So, this place is right on top
of a natural safety net.

85
00:04:52,667 --> 00:04:53,751
Then…

86
00:04:54,335 --> 00:04:56,421
Yes, exactly.

87
00:04:57,046 --> 00:05:01,342
If you bring the humans here
before the landslide happens,

88
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,760
they will all survive.

89
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:05,054
Hey there!

90
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,264
Wait a minute.

91
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:08,182
Hey.

92
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,852
You're a Grim Reaper, right?

93
00:05:11,602 --> 00:05:14,272
Are you sure you should be doing this?

94
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:18,276
It's fine.

95
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,278
I have already…

96
00:05:22,363 --> 00:05:23,614
worked enough.

97
00:06:10,119 --> 00:06:14,248
As expected, the calm earlier on the shore
was the calm before the storm.

98
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:16,250
It is very windy here now!

99
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:19,962
-Do not go outside during this storm!
-It sounds real bad!

100
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:22,340
-It's impressive.
-Please seek shelter inside!

101
00:06:22,423 --> 00:06:24,217
The wind is getting stronger.

102
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,302
Yeah. It will be okay, right?

103
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:28,513
This house won't get blown away, right?

104
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:30,973
I think it's quite well built.

105
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:35,103
Just in case there's a blackout,
we have a flashlight!

106
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:39,232
But when its battery runs out,
let's kiss again, Rinrin!

107
00:06:40,608 --> 00:06:42,902
-We have this lamp too.
-Oh, nice!

108
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:45,780
Camping stuff is so useful
for times like this.

109
00:06:45,863 --> 00:06:47,990
I should charge my phone now!

110
00:06:48,074 --> 00:06:49,242
Rinrin, here.

111
00:06:50,034 --> 00:06:53,329
I should also move the stuff
in the fridge to the cooler.

112
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:55,164
I'll go check a few things.

113
00:07:00,002 --> 00:07:01,295
We've got a problem!

114
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,296
What is it?

115
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:05,049
I just noticed we have quite a leak here!

116
00:07:05,133 --> 00:07:07,593
-A leak? Wait a minute.
-Yeah.

117
00:07:08,928 --> 00:07:09,846
Use these.

118
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,806
Yeah, okay.

119
00:07:21,899 --> 00:07:23,359
Mr. Nishigami?

120
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:26,779
Everyone, let's get out of here.

121
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,994
We are going out in this weather?

122
00:07:33,077 --> 00:07:35,121
-It's dangerous to stay here.
-Oh, no!

123
00:07:35,204 --> 00:07:36,038
Rinrin, you okay?

124
00:07:36,122 --> 00:07:38,499
-I can't get them on.
-Oh, I'm so wet!

125
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:40,960
They are hard to put on!

126
00:07:41,043 --> 00:07:43,212
-The oranges!
-Hurry up!

127
00:07:43,796 --> 00:07:47,675
The velcro… the velcro's not sticking!

128
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:53,222
They're being blown away!

129
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,170
Mr. Nishigami.

130
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:27,089
What are you doing? It's dangerous here.

131
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:30,468
What if something happens to you?

132
00:08:31,469 --> 00:08:32,595
Mr. Nishigami!

133
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:35,139
Please, help me pick the oranges.

134
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:18,307
I…

135
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:22,478
have met you before.

136
00:09:24,397 --> 00:09:25,439
Thank you.

137
00:09:36,325 --> 00:09:37,410
Come on.

138
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:39,287
This place isn't safe.

139
00:09:39,829 --> 00:09:40,830
Let's go.

140
00:09:48,629 --> 00:09:49,714
Jeez…

141
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:53,759
He really went and did it.

142
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:11,694
This is going to turn into quite a storm.

143
00:10:13,529 --> 00:10:15,740
No matter how much AI evolves,

144
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:17,825
it can't stop a typhoon.
Isn't it powerless?

145
00:10:18,993 --> 00:10:22,288
This storm really
makes you feel the limits of AI.

146
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:24,832
I wonder if that villa is okay?

147
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:28,461
A direct hit on Tatsumi Town?

148
00:10:29,712 --> 00:10:32,798
That villa was built
on a slope facing the sea.

149
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:36,886
I hope it isn't damaged.

150
00:10:57,865 --> 00:11:03,746
DISASTER PREVENTION COMMITTEE

151
00:11:13,255 --> 00:11:17,051
Oh, no! I'm soaked!

152
00:11:17,134 --> 00:11:19,553
-Be careful! The rain is really pouring!
-I'm cold!

153
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:21,305
Everyone, get inside.

154
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:23,682
Tsumugi, hurry!

155
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,643
I thought I was going to die!

156
00:11:26,727 --> 00:11:29,188
-Wow!
-It's safe here.

157
00:11:30,147 --> 00:11:31,399
My grandma's ashes.

158
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:34,819
It's fine. We'll go back there
once the typhoon passes.

159
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,614
But…

160
00:11:39,156 --> 00:11:41,867
I feel like I shouldn't leave them there.

161
00:11:43,953 --> 00:11:44,995
I'll go get them.

162
00:11:45,663 --> 00:11:46,622
What?

163
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:50,751
Mr. Nishigami!

164
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,170
It's raining hard.

165
00:11:53,254 --> 00:11:55,506
Are you going down
that mountain path again?

166
00:11:57,925 --> 00:11:59,009
Why…

167
00:12:01,178 --> 00:12:05,224
Why do so much for me?

168
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,064
I…

169
00:12:13,315 --> 00:12:14,942
have met you before.

170
00:12:20,614 --> 00:12:21,824
Who are you?

171
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:36,422
Ms. Midori.

172
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,175
This summer

173
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:42,136
was the best vacation.

174
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:43,888
Thank you.

175
00:12:48,559 --> 00:12:49,560
I…

176
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:54,273
I like you,

177
00:12:55,649 --> 00:12:56,734
Mr. Nishigami.

178
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:00,946
Me too.

179
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:04,617
I like you, Ms. Midori.

180
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,578
And I probably will…

181
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:10,956
forever.

182
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:49,495
Goodbye.

183
00:14:00,339 --> 00:14:01,507
Mr. Nishigami…

184
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:35,291
You came

185
00:14:36,834 --> 00:14:38,919
to save me too, didn't you?

186
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:41,547
Yes.

187
00:14:42,631 --> 00:14:45,259
Sorry for forgetting you.

188
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,932
Thank you, Mr. Nishigami.

189
00:14:53,183 --> 00:14:56,353
For saving those children.

190
00:15:03,861 --> 00:15:07,865
A Grim Reaper, saving humans…

191
00:15:14,663 --> 00:15:17,708
It's the opposite
of what I should be doing.

192
00:15:23,839 --> 00:15:25,174
But I feel like

193
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:32,514
the reason I kept being a Reaper
was to save them someday.

194
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:38,979
You gave them a second chance at life.

195
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:45,486
I'm sure they will do their best
to not waste it.

196
00:15:56,288 --> 00:15:59,291
Goodbye, Mr. Nishigami!

197
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:18,602
The best vacation…

198
00:16:32,866 --> 00:16:34,034
Thank you…

199
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:36,704
everyone.

200
00:17:25,878 --> 00:17:26,754
What?

201
00:17:27,379 --> 00:17:28,672
We…

202
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:33,343
You've done something terrible.

203
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:35,804
I erased those humans' memories.

204
00:17:35,888 --> 00:17:37,806
Is this where the villa was?

205
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:39,391
The villa is gone!

206
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:41,935
No one remembers you anymore.

207
00:17:42,519 --> 00:17:46,023
Is God telling us
that our vacation is over?

208
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,984
Why did it come to this?

209
00:17:49,568 --> 00:17:53,739
Your human form has become grains of sand,
turned into sea foam,

210
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,575
and vanished.

211
00:17:57,951 --> 00:17:58,911
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
